### <a id="vuln-03"></a>[VULN-03] Universal Anti-CSRF Token Bypass in Moderator Panel (`$token = true`)

> [!NOTE]
> **Audit Occurrence Disclaimer:** Found in **8 of 9** available audit reports (`8e693d74`, `3643eaa6`, `6bb7274b`, `88c733dd`, `c6fa5ed1`, `a3b97157`, `5e432690`, `991dcf68`).

| Specification | Metric / Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Vulnerability Identifier** | `VULN-03` |
| **Severity Level** | **🔴 Critical** |
| **Vulnerability Classification** | CWE-352 (Cross-Site Request Forgery), CVSS 9.8 (Critical) |
| **Primary Target Locations** | `Repository-wide` |

#### Technical Description & Exploit Mechanics

In `mod.php`, anti-CSRF token verification is intentionally broken by a hardcoded variable override:
  ```php
  $token = true;
  if ($token != make_secure_link_token($action)) {
      error($config['error']['csrf']);
  }
  ```
  Because comparison uses PHP loose inequality (`!=`), the boolean `true` comparison coerces the HMAC returned by `make_secure_link_token()` into a boolean (`(bool)"any_non_empty_string" === true`). Thus, `true != true` evaluates to `false`, completely bypassing token validation for any state-changing moderator action.

