| **Primary Target Locations** | `Repository-wide` |

#### Technical Description & Exploit Mechanics

The web configuration editor serializes config updates into PHP code and writes them to disk (`file_put_contents`):
  ```php
  // inc/mod/pages.php
  $config_code = "<?php\n// Generated by " . $mod['username'] . "\n" . $_POST['code'];
  file_put_contents($config_file, $config_code);
  shell_exec_error('php -l ' . $config_file);
  ```
  If an attacker creates an account with PHP delimiters in the username (e.g. `test\n*/ system($_GET['c']); /*`), or passes unescaped PHP code via `$_POST['code']` (facilitated by the CSRF bypass in Finding 3), arbitrary code is written to `inc/secrets.php` or board config files, executing on every subsequent HTTP request.

